  "id": "conflict-behavior",
  "term": "conflict behavior",
  "definition": "Conflict behavior is group action that arises when people see different social classes as having opposed interests. In the class context described here, it often refers to collective actions by lower-status groups, such as protests, strikes, or other rights-claiming actions driven by unmet material interests, power concerns, or needs for respect.",
